IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb4-common`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part XV, ss 173 to 180: AMENDMENT OF ARTICLES.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice Canada consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. How a corporation's articles (the document that sets out its name, share classes
-- and rights) are amended: what may be amended by special resolution (s 173), how a distributing
-- corporation may constrain who owns its shares (s 174), who may propose an amendment and what the notice
-- must say (s 175), when a class or series of shares votes separately (s 176), and the steps that follow:
-- articles of amendment sent to the Director (s 177), certificate (s 178), effect (s 179), restating the
-- articles (s 180). Provisions that tell the Director what to do are encoded for what they decide for the
-- corporation and its people: whether the duty arises, and from when the change takes effect.
--
-- Not in this module: the form the Director fixes and the contents of the certificate (s 262, piece cb5).
-- Dates are asked as DATEs; the Act fixes no date in this range.

§ `Part XV -- Fundamental Changes`

§§ `s 173 Amendment of articles`

-- "Special resolution" is the keel's `special resolution within s 2(1)`: two-thirds or more of the votes
-- cast by the shareholders who voted, or a resolution signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote.
-- "Subject to sections 176 and 177": s 176 adds a separate vote by each class or series entitled to vote
-- separately, and s 177 sends the articles of amendment to the Director; both are encoded below, and the
-- rule `the amendment is adopted within s 173(1) and s 176(6)` puts the two votes together (fork F1).
-- src:2098 | 173 (1) Subject to sections 176 and 177, the articles of a corporation may by special resolution be amended to
-- src:2099 | (a) change its name;
-- src:2100 | (b) change the province in which its registered office is situated;
-- src:2101 | (c) add, change or remove any restriction on the business or businesses that the corporation may carry on;
-- src:2102 | (d) change any maximum number of shares that the corporation is authorized to issue;
-- src:2103 | (e) create new classes of shares;
-- src:2104 | (f) reduce or increase its stated capital, if its stated capital is set out in the articles;
-- src:2105 | (g) change the designation of all or any of its shares, and add, change or remove any rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions, including rights to accrued dividends, in respect of all or any of its shares, whether issued or unissued;
-- src:2106 | (h) change the shares of any class or series, whether issued or unissued, into a different number of shares of the same class or series or into the same or a different number of shares of other classes or series;
-- src:2107 | (i) divide a class of shares, whether issued or unissued, into series and fix the number of shares in each series and the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions thereof;
-- src:2108 | (j) authorize the directors to divide any class of unissued shares into series and fix the number of shares in each series and the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions thereof;
-- src:2109 | (k) authorize the directors to change the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attached to unissued shares of any series;
-- src:2110 | (l) revoke, diminish or enlarge any authority conferred under paragraphs (j) and (k);
-- src:2111 | (m) increase or decrease the number of directors or the minimum or maximum number of directors, subject to sections 107 and 112;
-- src:2112 | (n) add, change or remove restrictions on the issue, transfer or ownership of shares; or
-- src:2113 | (o) add, change or remove any other provision that is permitted by this Act to be set out in the articles.
@ref CBCA s 173(1) (src:2098-2113)
DECLARE `Kind of amendment under s 173(1)` IS ONE OF
    `to change the name (s 173(1)(a))`
    `to change the province of the registered office (s 173(1)(b))`
    `to add, change or remove a restriction on the business (s 173(1)(c))`
    `to change a maximum number of shares authorized (s 173(1)(d))`
    `to create new classes of shares (s 173(1)(e))`
    `to reduce or increase stated capital set out in the articles (s 173(1)(f))`
    `to change the designation of shares or their rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions (s 173(1)(g))`
    `to change shares into a different number of the same class or series or into other classes or series (s 173(1)(h))`
    `to divide a class of shares into series (s 173(1)(i))`
    `to authorize the directors to divide a class of unissued shares into series (s 173(1)(j))`
    `to authorize the directors to change the rights of unissued shares of a series (s 173(1)(k))`
    `to revoke, diminish or enlarge an authority under paragraph (j) or (k) (s 173(1)(l))`
    `to change the number of directors or the minimum or maximum number (s 173(1)(m))`
    `to add, change or remove restrictions on the issue, transfer or ownership of shares (s 173(1)(n))`
    `to add, change or remove any other provision permitted by this Act to be set out in the articles (s 173(1)(o))`
    `a change that s 173(1) does not list`

-- Three paragraphs carry a condition of their own: (f) only "if its stated capital is set out in the
-- articles", (m) "subject to sections 107 and 112" and (o) only for a provision "permitted by this Act to
-- be set out in the articles". Each is a plain input, read only for its own kind. A change that
-- paragraphs (a) to (o) do not list is not authorized by this subsection (it may be by another section,
-- for example s 173(3) or s 191); the rule answers for s 173(1) only.
@ref CBCA s 173(1) (src:2098-2113)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of amendment under s 173(1)`
      `the stated capital is set out in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: sections 107 and 112 (piece cb2)
      `the change complies with sections 107 and 112` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Act permits the provision to be set out in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      tally IS A `Vote tally`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles may be amended by special resolution within s 173(1)` MEANS
        `special resolution within s 2(1)` tally
    AND `the condition that the kind of amendment adds is met`
    WHERE
        `the condition that the kind of amendment adds is met` MEANS
            CONSIDER kind
            WHEN `to reduce or increase stated capital set out in the articles (s 173(1)(f))` THEN `the stated capital is set out in the articles`
            WHEN `to change the number of directors or the minimum or maximum number (s 173(1)(m))` THEN `the change complies with sections 107 and 112`
            WHEN `to add, change or remove any other provision permitted by this Act to be set out in the articles (s 173(1)(o))` THEN `this Act permits the provision to be set out in the articles`
            WHEN `a change that s 173(1) does not list` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The amendment is adopted only when the special resolution of the shareholders has passed AND, where s 176
-- gives a class or series a separate vote, each such class or series has approved it by a special
-- resolution (s 176(6)). `every class or series entitled to vote separately has approved` is TRUE when no
-- class or series is entitled to vote separately (fork F1: the class votes are in addition to the
-- general special resolution).
-- src:2175 | (6) A proposed amendment to the articles referred to in subsection (1) is adopted when the holders of the shares of each class or series entitled to vote separately thereon as a class or series have approved such amendment by a special resolution.
@ref CBCA s 173(1), s 176(6) (src:2098 src:2175)
GIVEN `the articles may be amended by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every class or series entitled to vote separately has approved by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the amendment is adopted within s 173(1) and s 176(6)` MEANS
        `the articles may be amended by special resolution`
    AND `every class or series entitled to vote separately has approved by special resolution`

-- src:2114 | Termination
-- src:2115 | (2) The directors of a corporation may, if authorized by the shareholders in the special resolution effecting an amendment under this section, revoke the resolution before it is acted on without further approval of the shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 173(2) (src:2115)
GIVEN `the special resolution authorized the directors to revoke it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution has been acted on` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may revoke the resolution without further approval of the shareholders within s 173(2)` MEANS
        `the special resolution authorized the directors to revoke it`
    AND (NOT `the resolution has been acted on`)

-- "Number name": a corporation whose name is a designating number (for example 1234567 Canada Inc.).
-- src:2116 | Amendment of number name
-- src:2117 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection (1), where a corporation has a designating number as a name, the directors may amend its articles to change that name to a verbal name.
@ref CBCA s 173(3) (src:2117)
GIVEN `the corporation has a designating number as a name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment changes that name to a verbal name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may amend the articles to change a number name within s 173(3)` MEANS
        `the corporation has a designating number as a name`
    AND `the amendment changes that name to a verbal name`

§§ `s 174 Constraints on shares`

-- A "constraint" limits who may be issued, transfer or own shares: for example a limit to Canadian
-- residents so that a licence or a grant can be kept. Only a distributing corporation (an "offering"
-- corporation, s 2(1)) may do it, and only for the purposes the subsection lists.
-- src:2118 | Constraints on shares
-- src:2119 | 174 (1) Subject to sections 176 and 177, a distributing corporation, any of the issued shares of which remain outstanding and are held by more than one person, may by special resolution amend its articles in accordance with the regulations to constrain
-- src:2120 | (a) the issue or transfer of shares of any class or series to persons who are not resident Canadians;
-- src:2121 | (b) the issue or transfer of shares of any class or series to enable the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to qualify under any prescribed law of Canada or a province
-- src:2122 | (i) to obtain a licence to carry on any business,
-- src:2123 | (ii) to become a publisher of a Canadian newspaper or periodical, or
-- src:2124 | (iii) to acquire shares of a financial intermediary as defined in the regulations;
-- src:2125 | (c) the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of any class or series in order to assist the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to qualify under any prescribed law of Canada or a province to receive licences, permits, grants, payments or other benefits by reason of attaining or maintaining a specified level of Canadian ownership or control;
-- src:2126 | (d) the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of any class or series in order to assist the corporation to comply with any prescribed law.
-- src:2127 | (e) the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of any class or series to enable the corporation to be a registered labour-sponsored venture capital corporation under Part X.3 of the Income Tax Act.
@ref CBCA s 174(1) (src:2119-2127)
DECLARE `Kind of constraint under s 174(1)` IS ONE OF
    `on the issue or transfer of shares to persons who are not resident Canadians (s 174(1)(a))`
    `on issue or transfer to qualify for a licence to carry on a business under a prescribed law (s 174(1)(b)(i))`
    `on issue or transfer to become a publisher of a Canadian newspaper or periodical under a prescribed law (s 174(1)(b)(ii))`
    `on issue or transfer to acquire shares of a financial intermediary under a prescribed law (s 174(1)(b)(iii))`
    `on issue, transfer or ownership to qualify for licences, permits, grants or benefits by a level of Canadian ownership or control (s 174(1)(c))`
    `on issue, transfer or ownership to comply with a prescribed law (s 174(1)(d))`
    `on issue, transfer or ownership to be a registered labour-sponsored venture capital corporation (s 174(1)(e))`
    `a constraint that s 174(1) does not list`

-- The facts about a proposed constraint, in one record. "Prescribed law": the laws prescribed by the
-- regulations are not among the sources, so whether the law concerned is one is a plain input.
-- "Held by more than one person" is asked as a fact about the outstanding issued shares.
@ref CBCA s 174(1) (src:2119-2127)
DECLARE `Proposed constraint on shares (s 174)` HAS
    `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `issued shares of the corporation remain outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `those outstanding shares are held by more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the constraint proposed` IS A `Kind of constraint under s 174(1)`
    `the law concerned is a prescribed law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amendment is made in accordance with the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shares of the class or series affected are outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `those shares are already subject to a constraint permitted under paragraph 174(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "Exception in respect of paragraph (1)(c)": a constraint of the (c) kind cannot be put on a class or
-- series of which any shares are outstanding unless those shares are already subject to such a constraint.
-- src:2128 | Exception in respect of paragraph (1)(c)
-- src:2129 | (2) Paragraph (1)(c) does not permit a constraint on the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of any class or series of which any shares are outstanding unless
-- src:2130 | (a) in the case of a constraint in respect of a class, the shares of the class, or
-- src:2131 | (b) in the case of a constraint in respect of a series, the shares of the series
-- src:2132 | are already subject to a constraint permitted under that paragraph.
@ref CBCA s 174(2) (src:2129-2132)
GIVEN proposal IS A `Proposed constraint on shares (s 174)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`paragraph 174(1)(c) permits a constraint on the class or series within s 174(2)` MEANS
        (NOT proposal's `shares of the class or series affected are outstanding`)
    OR  proposal's `those shares are already subject to a constraint permitted under paragraph 174(1)(c)`

-- "Subject to sections 176 and 177": the class vote of s 176(1)(h) and the articles of amendment of s 177
-- are encoded in their own sections. "In accordance with the regulations": a plain input.
@ref CBCA s 174(1), s 174(2) (src:2119-2127 src:2129-2132)
GIVEN proposal IS A `Proposed constraint on shares (s 174)`
      tally IS A `Vote tally`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may amend its articles to constrain shares by special resolution within s 174(1)` MEANS
        proposal's `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
    AND proposal's `issued shares of the corporation remain outstanding`
    AND proposal's `those outstanding shares are held by more than one person`
    AND proposal's `the amendment is made in accordance with the regulations`
    AND `special resolution within s 2(1)` tally
    AND `the purpose of the constraint is permitted`
    WHERE
        `the purpose of the constraint is permitted` MEANS
            CONSIDER proposal's `the constraint proposed`
            WHEN `on the issue or transfer of shares to persons who are not resident Canadians (s 174(1)(a))` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `on issue or transfer to qualify for a licence to carry on a business under a prescribed law (s 174(1)(b)(i))` THEN proposal's `the law concerned is a prescribed law`
            WHEN `on issue or transfer to become a publisher of a Canadian newspaper or periodical under a prescribed law (s 174(1)(b)(ii))` THEN proposal's `the law concerned is a prescribed law`
            WHEN `on issue or transfer to acquire shares of a financial intermediary under a prescribed law (s 174(1)(b)(iii))` THEN proposal's `the law concerned is a prescribed law`
            WHEN `on issue, transfer or ownership to qualify for licences, permits, grants or benefits by a level of Canadian ownership or control (s 174(1)(c))` THEN
                    proposal's `the law concerned is a prescribed law`
                AND `paragraph 174(1)(c) permits a constraint on the class or series within s 174(2)` proposal
            WHEN `on issue, transfer or ownership to comply with a prescribed law (s 174(1)(d))` THEN proposal's `the law concerned is a prescribed law`
            WHEN `on issue, transfer or ownership to be a registered labour-sponsored venture capital corporation (s 174(1)(e))` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a constraint that s 174(1) does not list` THEN FALSE

-- "Limitation on ownership of shares": under paragraph (1)(c) the corporation may cap the shares one
-- person may own, or bar ownership, where that person's ownership would adversely affect the corporation's
-- or an affiliate's ability to reach or keep a level of Canadian ownership or control that is specified in
-- the articles and equals or exceeds the level referred to in paragraph (1)(c).
-- src:2133 | Limitation on ownership of shares
-- src:2134 | (3) A corporation may, pursuant to paragraph (1)(c), limit the number of shares of that corporation that may be owned, or prohibit the ownership of shares, by any person whose ownership would adversely affect the ability of the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to attain or maintain a level of Canadian ownership or control specified in its articles that equals or exceeds a specified level referred to in paragraph (1)(c).
@ref CBCA s 174(3) (src:2134)
GIVEN `the limit or prohibition is made pursuant to paragraph 174(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's ownership would adversely affect the ability to attain or maintain the level` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the level is specified in the articles and equals or exceeds the specified level referred to in paragraph 174(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may limit or prohibit a person's ownership of shares within s 174(3)` MEANS
        `the limit or prohibition is made pursuant to paragraph 174(1)(c)`
    AND `the person's ownership would adversely affect the ability to attain or maintain the level`
    AND `the level is specified in the articles and equals or exceeds the specified level referred to in paragraph 174(1)(c)`

-- "A corporation referred to in subsection (1)": a distributing corporation with issued shares
-- outstanding held by more than one person.
-- src:2135 | Change or removal of constraint
-- src:2136 | (4) A corporation referred to in subsection (1) may by special resolution amend its articles to change or remove any constraint on the issue, transfer or ownership of its shares.
@ref CBCA s 174(4) (src:2136)
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `issued shares of the corporation remain outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those outstanding shares are held by more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN
      tally IS A `Vote tally`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may amend its articles to change or remove a constraint by special resolution within s 174(4)` MEANS
        `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
    AND `issued shares of the corporation remain outstanding`
    AND `those outstanding shares are held by more than one person`
    AND `special resolution within s 2(1)` tally

-- src:2137 | Termination
-- src:2138 | (5) The directors of a corporation may, if authorized by the shareholders in the special resolution effecting an amendment under subsection (1) or (4), revoke the resolution before it is acted on without further approval of the shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 174(5) (src:2138)
GIVEN `the special resolution authorized the directors to revoke it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution has been acted on` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may revoke the resolution without further approval of the shareholders within s 174(5)` MEANS
        `the special resolution authorized the directors to revoke it`
    AND (NOT `the resolution has been acted on`)

-- (6) Regulations: the Governor in Council's power to make regulations is machinery; see the coverage table.

-- "Validity of acts": a failure to comply with s 174 or the regulations does not by itself invalidate the
-- issue, transfer or act. Any other defect is not decided by this subsection: NOTHING.
-- src:2146 | Validity of acts
-- src:2147 | (7) An issue or a transfer of a share or an act of a corporation is valid notwithstanding any failure to comply with this section or the regulations.
@ref CBCA s 174(7) (src:2147)
GIVEN `the only defect is a failure to comply with section 174 or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the issue, transfer or act is valid despite a failure to comply with s 174 within s 174(7)` MEANS
    IF `the only defect is a failure to comply with section 174 or the regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 175 Proposal to amend`

-- out of range: section 137 (piece cb3)
-- src:2148 | Proposal to amend
-- src:2149 | 175 (1) Subject to subsection (2), a director or a shareholder who is entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders may, in accordance with section 137, make a proposal to amend the articles.
@ref CBCA s 175(1) (src:2149)
GIVEN `the person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal is made in accordance with section 137` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person may make a proposal to amend the articles within s 175(1)` MEANS
        (    `the person is a director`
         OR  `the person is a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders`)
    AND `the proposal is made in accordance with section 137`

-- "Where applicable": the notice must state the dissent right only where s 190 gives one for this
-- amendment. The duty falls on the corporation sending the notice (s 135, piece cb3, governs the notice
-- itself).
-- src:2150 | Notice of amendment
-- src:2151 | (2) Notice of a meeting of shareholders at which a proposal to amend the articles is to be considered shall set out the proposed amendment and, where applicable, shall state that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190, but failure to make that statement does not invalidate an amendment.
@ref CBCA s 175(2) (src:2151)
GIVEN `the notice sets out the proposed amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice of the meeting complies within s 175(2)` MEANS
        `the notice sets out the proposed amendment`
    AND (    (NOT `a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares in accordance with section 190`)
         OR  `the notice states that a dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of their shares`)

@ref CBCA s 175(2) (src:2151)
GIVEN `the omission of the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Effect on validity of leaving out the dissent statement`
`the effect on the amendment of leaving out the dissent statement within s 175(2)` MEANS
    `the effect of leaving out the dissent statement` `the omission of the dissent statement was the only failure of the notice`

§§ `s 176 Class vote`

-- "Class vote": the holders of one class (or series) of shares vote on their own, apart from the
-- shareholders as a whole, on an amendment that touches their class in the ways paragraphs (a) to (h)
-- list. Paragraph (c) says "without limiting the generality of the foregoing" and lists four examples
-- ((i) to (iv)); the examples are inside (c) and add no case of their own.
-- src:2153 | 176 (1) The holders of shares of a class or, subject to subsection (4), of a series are, unless the articles otherwise provide in the case of an amendment referred to in paragraphs (a), (b) and (e), entitled to vote separately as a class or series on a proposal to amend the articles to
-- src:2154 | (a) increase or decrease any maximum number of authorized shares of such class, or increase any maximum number of authorized shares of a class having rights or privileges equal or superior to the shares of such class;
-- src:2155 | (b) effect an exchange, reclassification or cancellation of all or part of the shares of such class;
-- src:2156 | (c) add, change or remove the rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached to the shares of such class and, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
-- src:2157 | (i) remove or change prejudicially rights to accrued dividends or rights to cumulative dividends,
-- src:2158 | (ii) add, remove or change prejudicially redemption rights,
-- src:2159 | (iii) reduce or remove a dividend preference or a liquidation preference, or
-- src:2160 | (iv) add, remove or change prejudicially conversion privileges, options, voting, transfer or pre-emptive rights, or rights to acquire securities of a corporation, or sinking fund provisions;
-- src:2161 | (d) increase the rights or privileges of any class of shares having rights or privileges equal or superior to the shares of such class;
-- src:2162 | (e) create a new class of shares equal or superior to the shares of such class;
-- src:2163 | (f) make any class of shares having rights or privileges inferior to the shares of such class equal or superior to the shares of such class;
-- src:2164 | (g) effect an exchange or create a right of exchange of all or part of the shares of another class into the shares of such class; or
-- src:2165 | (h) constrain the issue, transfer or ownership of the shares of such class or change or remove such constraint.
@ref CBCA s 176(1) (src:2153-2165)
DECLARE `Effect of a proposed amendment on a class of shares (s 176(1))` IS ONE OF
    `an increase or decrease of a maximum number of authorized shares of the class, or an increase for an equal or superior class (s 176(1)(a))`
    `an exchange, reclassification or cancellation of all or part of the shares of the class (s 176(1)(b))`
    `a change to the rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached to the shares of the class (s 176(1)(c))`
    `an increase of the rights or privileges of a class with equal or superior rights or privileges (s 176(1)(d))`
    `the creation of a new class equal or superior to the class (s 176(1)(e))`
    `making a class with inferior rights or privileges equal or superior to the class (s 176(1)(f))`
    `an exchange, or a right of exchange, of shares of another class into shares of the class (s 176(1)(g))`
    `a constraint on the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of the class, or a change or removal of it (s 176(1)(h))`
    `no effect that s 176(1) lists`

-- Whether the holders of the class are entitled to the separate vote. "Unless the articles otherwise
-- provide in the case of an amendment referred to in paragraphs (a), (b) and (e)": only those three can be
-- displaced by the articles. Subsection (3) deems a new class that is constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c)
-- and otherwise equal not to be "equal or superior" for paragraph (e). Subsection (2) removes a proposal
-- that only adds a right to convert into such a class. The series rule of subsection (4) is separate, below.
-- src:2166 | Exception
-- src:2167 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply in respect of a proposal to amend the articles to add a right or privilege for a holder to convert shares of a class or series into shares of another class or series that is subject to a constraint permitted under paragraph 174(1)(c) but is otherwise equal to the class or series first mentioned.
-- src:2168 | Deeming provision
-- src:2169 | (3) For the purpose of paragraph (1)(e), a new class of shares, the issue, transfer or ownership of which is to be constrained by an amendment to the articles pursuant to paragraph 174(1)(c), that is otherwise equal to an existing class of shares shall be deemed not to be equal or superior to the existing class of shares.
@ref CBCA s 176(1), s 176(2), s 176(3) (src:2153-2165 src:2167 src:2169)
GIVEN effect IS A `Effect of a proposed amendment on a class of shares (s 176(1))`
      `the articles provide that the holders may not vote separately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new class would be constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c) and is otherwise equal to the class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment only adds a right to convert into an otherwise equal class constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the holders of the class are entitled to vote separately as a class within s 176(1)` MEANS
        (NOT `the amendment only adds a right to convert into an otherwise equal class constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c)`)
    AND `the effect entitles the holders`
    WHERE
        `the effect entitles the holders` MEANS
            CONSIDER effect
            WHEN `an increase or decrease of a maximum number of authorized shares of the class, or an increase for an equal or superior class (s 176(1)(a))` THEN NOT `the articles provide that the holders may not vote separately`
            WHEN `an exchange, reclassification or cancellation of all or part of the shares of the class (s 176(1)(b))` THEN NOT `the articles provide that the holders may not vote separately`
            WHEN `a change to the rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached to the shares of the class (s 176(1)(c))` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an increase of the rights or privileges of a class with equal or superior rights or privileges (s 176(1)(d))` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the creation of a new class equal or superior to the class (s 176(1)(e))` THEN
                    (NOT `the articles provide that the holders may not vote separately`)
                AND (NOT `the new class would be constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c) and is otherwise equal to the class`)
            WHEN `making a class with inferior rights or privileges equal or superior to the class (s 176(1)(f))` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an exchange, or a right of exchange, of shares of another class into shares of the class (s 176(1)(g))` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a constraint on the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of the class, or a change or removal of it (s 176(1)(h))` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `no effect that s 176(1) lists` THEN FALSE

-- A separate vote by a SERIES of a class lies "only if such series is affected by an amendment in a
-- manner different from other shares of the same class".
-- src:2170 | Limitation
-- src:2171 | (4) The holders of a series of shares of a class are entitled to vote separately as a series under subsection (1) only if such series is affected by an amendment in a manner different from other shares of the same class.
@ref CBCA s 176(4) (src:2171)
GIVEN `the holders hold a series of shares of a class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the series is affected in a manner different from other shares of the same class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the holders of a series are entitled to vote separately as a series within s 176(4)` MEANS
        `the holders hold a series of shares of a class`
    AND `the series is affected in a manner different from other shares of the same class`

-- A class OR a series: the holders of a series have the separate vote only if both subsection (1) gives
-- it and subsection (4) allows it. Used by s 183(4), which asks whether a provision "would entitle such
-- holders to vote as a class or series under section 176".
@ref CBCA s 176(1), s 176(4) (src:2153-2165 src:2171)
GIVEN effect IS A `Effect of a proposed amendment on a class of shares (s 176(1))`
      `the articles provide that the holders may not vote separately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new class would be constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c) and is otherwise equal to the class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment only adds a right to convert into an otherwise equal class constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holders hold a series of shares of a class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the series is affected in a manner different from other shares of the same class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the holders of a class or series are entitled to vote separately within s 176(1) and s 176(4)` MEANS
        `the holders of the class are entitled to vote separately as a class within s 176(1)` effect `the articles provide that the holders may not vote separately` `the new class would be constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c) and is otherwise equal to the class` `the amendment only adds a right to convert into an otherwise equal class constrained under paragraph 174(1)(c)`
    AND (    (NOT `the holders hold a series of shares of a class`)
         OR  `the holders of a series are entitled to vote separately as a series within s 176(4)` `the holders hold a series of shares of a class` `the series is affected in a manner different from other shares of the same class`)

-- "Whether or not shares of a class or series otherwise carry the right to vote": the separate vote does
-- not depend on whether the shares carry a vote at general meetings. The shares' ordinary voting right is
-- read by no part of the answer (a test shows that changing it changes nothing).
-- src:2172 | Right to vote
-- src:2173 | (5) Subsection (1) applies whether or not shares of a class or series otherwise carry the right to vote.
@ref CBCA s 176(5) (src:2173)
GIVEN `the holders are entitled to vote separately under subsection 176(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares otherwise carry the right to vote` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the holders may vote separately even if the shares carry no other vote within s 176(5)` MEANS
    `the holders are entitled to vote separately under subsection 176(1)`

-- "Separate resolutions": the amendment is adopted when the holders of each class or series entitled to
-- vote separately have approved it by a special resolution. One tally per class or series.
@ref CBCA s 176(6) (src:2175)
GIVEN tallies IS A LIST OF `Vote tally`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every class or series entitled to vote separately has approved within s 176(6)` MEANS
    `every tally in the list passes as a special resolution` tallies

§§ `s 177 Delivery of articles` 

-- src:2176 | Delivery of articles
-- src:2177 | 177 (1) Subject to any revocation under subsection 173(2) or 174(5), after an amendment has been adopted under section 173, 174 or 176 articles of amendment in the form that the Director fixes shall be sent to the Director.
@ref CBCA s 177(1) (src:2177)
GIVEN `an amendment has been adopted under section 173, 174 or 176` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have revoked the resolution under subsection 173(2) or 174(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must send articles of amendment to the Director within s 177(1)` MEANS
        `an amendment has been adopted under section 173, 174 or 176`
    AND (NOT `the directors have revoked the resolution under subsection 173(2) or 174(5)`)

-- Subsections 38(3) and (4) (piece cb1) govern the reduction; whether they are met is theirs.
-- src:2178 | Reduction of stated capital
-- src:2179 | (2) If an amendment effects or requires a reduction of stated capital, subsections 38(3) and (4) apply.
@ref CBCA s 177(2) (src:2179)
GIVEN `the amendment effects or requires a reduction of stated capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subsections 38(3) and (4) apply to the amendment within s 177(2)` MEANS
    `the amendment effects or requires a reduction of stated capital`

§§ `s 178 Certificate of amendment`

-- The Director's duty, encoded for what it means to the corporation: on receipt the certificate follows.
-- The form and issue "in accordance with section 262" are piece cb5's.
-- src:2180 | Certificate of amendment
-- src:2181 | 178 On receipt of articles of amendment, the Director shall issue a certificate of amendment in accordance with section 262.
@ref CBCA s 178 (src:2181)
GIVEN `the Director has received articles of amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must issue a certificate of amendment within s 178` MEANS
    `the Director has received articles of amendment`

§§ `s 179 Effect of certificate`

-- src:2182 | Effect of certificate
-- src:2183 | 179 (1) An amendment becomes effective on the date shown in the certificate of amendment and the articles are amended accordingly.
@ref CBCA s 179(1) (src:2183)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the amendment is effective and the articles stand amended on a day within s 179(1)` MEANS
    `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the date shown in the certificate of amendment`

-- The protected matters are: an existing cause of action, claim, or liability to prosecution in favour of
-- or against the corporation or its directors or officers, and any civil, criminal or administrative
-- action or proceeding to which the corporation or its directors or officers is a party. Any other matter
-- is not decided by this subsection (NOTHING).
-- src:2184 | Rights preserved
-- src:2185 | (2) No amendment to the articles affects an existing cause of action or claim or liability to prosecution in favour of or against the corporation or its directors or officers, or any civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding to which a corporation or its directors or officers is a party.
@ref CBCA s 179(2) (src:2185)
GIVEN `the matter is an existing cause of action, claim, liability to prosecution, or an action or proceeding to which the corporation or its directors or officers is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`whether a matter is unaffected by an amendment within s 179(2)` MEANS
    `whether a listed matter is unaffected` `the matter is an existing cause of action, claim, liability to prosecution, or an action or proceeding to which the corporation or its directors or officers is a party`

§§ `s 180 Restated articles`

DECLARE `Directors' position on restating the articles` IS ONE OF
    `the directors may restate the articles at any time and are not required to`
    `the directors must restate the articles`

-- src:2186 | Restated articles
-- src:2187 | 180 (1) The directors may at any time, and shall when reasonably so directed by the Director, restate the articles of incorporation.
@ref CBCA s 180(1) (src:2187)
GIVEN `the Director has reasonably directed the directors to restate the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Directors' position on restating the articles`
`the directors' position on restating the articles within s 180(1)` MEANS
    IF `the Director has reasonably directed the directors to restate the articles`
    THEN `the directors must restate the articles`
    ELSE `the directors may restate the articles at any time and are not required to`

-- src:2188 | Delivery of articles
-- src:2189 | (2) Restated articles of incorporation in the form that the Director fixes shall be sent to the Director.
@ref CBCA s 180(2) (src:2189)
GIVEN `the articles of incorporation have been restated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the restated articles must be sent to the Director within s 180(2)` MEANS
    `the articles of incorporation have been restated`

-- src:2190 | Restated certificate
-- src:2191 | (3) On receipt of restated articles of incorporation, the Director shall issue a restated certificate of incorporation in accordance with section 262.
@ref CBCA s 180(3) (src:2191)
GIVEN `the Director has received restated articles of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must issue a restated certificate of incorporation within s 180(3)` MEANS
    `the Director has received restated articles of incorporation`

-- "Supersede": from the date shown, the restated articles replace the original articles and every
-- amendment of them.
-- src:2192 | Effect of certificate
-- src:2193 | (4) Restated articles of incorporation are effective on the date shown in the restated certificate of incorporation and supersede the original articles of incorporation and all amendments thereto.
@ref CBCA s 180(4) (src:2193)
GIVEN `the date shown in the restated certificate of incorporation` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the restated articles are effective and supersede the earlier articles on a day within s 180(4)` MEANS
    `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the date shown in the restated certificate of incorporation`
